WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.950
- Today we're gonna talk about Disney+.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.030
This was actually a really
wildly requested video.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.840
So many of you guys have been Tweeting me,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.330
leaving me comments asking me

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.550
what are my thoughts on Disney+.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:10.900
Am I going to subscribe?

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.290
What shows am I watching?

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.320
And what do I think.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.380
And obviously I'm a huge Disney fan.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.540
It's something that so
many of us grew up with

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:22.090
and just the nostalgia factor
of Disney+ alone is amazing.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.287
A huge thank you to Disney
for sponsoring this video.

00:00:24.287 --> 00:00:26.750
When I first logged in to Disney+,

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.640
it was just like this wave of emotions,

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.040
and I saw so many shows that I had watched

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.060
when I was younger.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.360
For example, one of the
shows that I recently watched

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.730
that was from my childhood,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.510
I remember so distinctly
watching this old version

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.720
of Shaggy Dog with my family,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.980
and it was weird watching it

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.050
because I had the same feelings that I had

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:44.883
when I was younger.

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:47.230
So it was kind of bring
back all of these memories.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.470
And it's so cool that Disney
has such an expansive library.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.840
And it's not just Disney that
you're getting access to.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.710
Pixar, Marvel, Star Wars,
National Geographic,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.010
and so much more.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.630
It's sort of overwhelming,

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.210
but in the best possible way.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:02.660
Disney+ is $6.99.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.398
Or if you wanna just buy
the whole year, it's $69.99.

00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:06.780
I'm gonna put a link in the description

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.880
where you guys can get
a seven day free trial.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:09.713
Check it out

00:01:09.713 --> 00:01:11.460
and I just wanna know what you guys think

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.930
because I have been having the best time.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.318
I've been so busy over the past few weeks

00:01:16.318 --> 00:01:18.790
and I've been traveling
a lot which is great

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.330
because I love watching content on flights

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.950
because that's usually my
time to just kind of hang out.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.570
And if I don't have any videos to edit,

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.010
I'm looking for content to watch.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.510
And what's great is you can
still have this stuff offline.

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:32.240
So you can download the shows
and take them on the go.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.620
Most planes do have wifi,

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.810
but you definitely
don't wanna rely on wifi

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.320
to watch any content ever.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.750
Just be sure to download it before I go.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.291
And I'm sure many of you guys are probably

00:01:41.291 --> 00:01:42.412
traveling for the holidays.

00:01:42.412 --> 00:01:43.277
And if you're not,

00:01:43.277 --> 00:01:44.320
I'm sure there's gonna
be some holiday downtime.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.470
So this could not be a more perfect time

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.270
to watch a lot of content.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.790
Another thing that is really great

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.340
is it's available on so
many different platforms.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.660
When I was traveling back from Nashville

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:56.920
I knew that I had about like
a four and a half ish flight,

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.280
and this was the day that
Disney+ had launched.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.280
So in that flight, before we took off

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.370
I watched the first
episode of The Mandalorian.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:06.980
I watched Encore, I
watched Lady in the Tramp.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:07.870
It was really cool to see,

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.050
because obviously I have a dog

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.790
and I love my dog more than anything.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.970
So to see these dogs
interacting with each other

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:15.367
and having real, genuine
conversations and feelings.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:18.153
I mean I have conversations
with my dog all the time,

00:02:18.153 --> 00:02:20.860
but to see that in like an updated version

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.300
of Lady in the Tramp was pretty great.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.800
I also watched The Imagineering Story.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.363
- [Narrator] Walt set a standard early on

00:02:27.363 --> 00:02:28.450
with The Imagineering.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:29.283
- This is such a fun show

00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:31.450
that covers a bunch of amazing
moments in Disney history.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.170
You get to meet a lot of incredible people

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.590
who helped bring so many
creative ideas to life.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.560
There's just so many great shows.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.090
Another show that I was so
surprised by was Encore.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.708
I'm not really like the
biggest fan of Broadway

00:02:42.708 --> 00:02:43.990
or like plays.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.050
I enjoy them, but it's not something

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.470
that I go out of my way to watch.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.820
So in preparing for my review
I watched the first episode

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.730
and it made me almost cry.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.160
The premise of the show
is a bunch of adults

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.180
who kind of go back to recreate
their high school plays.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.210
The first one was Annie

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.360
and they did such a great job storytelling

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.740
because a lot of these people

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.530
obviously aren't professional actors.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.190
So they were able to pull
so many great stories

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.023
out of these people.

00:03:07.023 --> 00:03:08.725
Kristen Bell is one of the
executive producers of the show

00:03:08.725 --> 00:03:10.980
so obviously I had to give it a shot

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.760
because I'm such a huge
fan of hers as well.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.660
The second episode

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.240
is the Beauty in the Beast episode

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.670
which was also really good.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.746
And they have all kinds of Disney movies.

00:03:18.746 --> 00:03:20.870
I mean they even have The Simpsons.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.778
Scrolling through to see
some of my other favorites.

00:03:23.778 --> 00:03:26.230
They also have some cute
little Pixar shorts.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.490
There's one where it's
Forky from Toy Story 4,

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.340
which is probably, I think,

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.070
now one of my favorite movies of all time.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.860
Everything about Toy
Story 4 was incredible.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.760
The story, the characters,
it's just so good.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.770
Oh My Gosh, Zenon, Girl
of the 21st Century.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:44.500
If I was able to be a
Disney star at one point,

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.120
I think this probably would've been me.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.127
The description is "2049 and teen Zenon

00:03:50.127 --> 00:03:52.537
"happily lives on an
orbiting space station.

00:03:52.537 --> 00:03:54.177
"When her curiosity gets her in trouble

00:03:54.177 --> 00:03:55.975
"she's sent to Earth for punishment

00:03:55.975 --> 00:03:56.808
"and needs to learn how to fit in."

00:03:56.808 --> 00:03:57.641
This is amazing

00:03:57.641 --> 00:03:59.170
because I feel like I'm
related so much to this show.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:03.150
Hannah Montana, Boy Meets
World, that's so amazing!

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.126
I think for how much you're paying

00:04:05.126 --> 00:04:06.640
and what you're getting

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.670
this is such an amazing deal,
especially for families.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:10.920
And the fact that you can just download it

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.720
and take it on the go is really great.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.320
I also watched Turner &amp; Hooch.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.157
I kinda was going back to all
of the shows that I watched

00:04:16.157 --> 00:04:17.460
when I was younger.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.587
1989!

00:04:18.587 --> 00:04:22.280
I was five.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.920
I just realized that I
didn't even get a chance

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.910
to really talk about The Mandalorian yet.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.610
I cannot believe how
incredible this show is.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.710
I mean obviously it's Star
Wars and I love Star Wars.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:33.360
I love the entire world with Star Wars.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.390
But this show, there's
something so special about it.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.220
I wish that I was filming my reaction

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.676
because when I got towards
the end of the first episode,

00:04:40.676 --> 00:04:45.676
I just (gasps) could not believe my eyes

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:47.810
and what I was seeing.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.360
And the best thing is
I avoided all spoilers.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.960
I didn't read any reviews.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.810
I wanted to go into this knowing nothing.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.870
I didn't even watch any of the trailers.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.830
I avoided absolutely everything,

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.570
so this experience for me was so great.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:02.060
I look forward to hearing
what you reaction was to it

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:03.740
and I cannot wait to see what happens

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:04.970
in the rest of these episodes.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.690
The character that I'm referencing

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:09.180
that you don't know what I'm talking about

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:11.140
unless you do know what I'm talking about

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:13.423
has made me cry every single episode.

00:05:13.423 --> 00:05:15.800
This character is extremely cute.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.270
That is all I'm gonna say

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:18.590
because I don't wanna give anything away.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:21.610
But oh geez, it's amazing, it's so great.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.569
This is kinda my first impressions.

00:05:23.569 --> 00:05:25.440
I guess it's not really first impressions

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.140
since I've watched hours and
hours of content at this point.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.820
And this could not be a more
perfect streaming platform

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.640
for people who are fans
of Disney and Pixar

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:33.680
and Star Wars and Marvel.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.240
It has everything that we love.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.400
Disney+ is offering people
a seven day free trial,

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.470
so I've put a link in the description

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:39.440
if you wanna check it out.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.369
I'm gonna go watch the latest Encore.

00:05:42.369 --> 00:05:43.463
See ya later.

